      "body": "## Motivation\n\nDeepSeek-V4 prefill CP gathers the whole chunk onto every CP rank before caching it (`cp_materialize_global_token_order` in `deepseek_v4.py` and `dsv4/compressor.py`), so all attention CP ranks hold byte-identical pages. The UMBP direct linker drops the TP term for such rank-replicated pools but keeps `cp{attn_cp_rank}` in every key, so the tier stores `attn_cp_size` copies of each page.\n\nWith PCP4, the UMBP linker logs a different suffix per CP rank (`cp0_pp0` .. `cp3_pp0`) for byte-identical pages.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. This PR: the UMBP direct linker shares one key across CP ranks for DeepSeek-V4.\n2. Mooncake direct linker: its single-writer rule (`tp_rank == 0`) must cover CP first. Follow-up.\n3. DSA (DeepSeek-V3.2 / GLM): stays per CP rank until its CP replication is verified. Follow-up.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `DevicePoolGroup` gets `cp_replicated` (default `False`); only the DeepSeek-V4 group sets it.\n- UMBP `_storage_suffix` uses `cp0` for such groups, so non-CP keys are unchanged and CP and non-CP deployments share pages.\n- Every rank still writes; a shared tier keeps one copy per key (`kSuccessAlreadyExists` in mori `page_backend.cpp`). CP ranks already agree on the hit length via `_all_reduce_attn_groups`.\n\n## Tests\n\n`test_umbp_direct_linker_rank_keys.py` and `test_linker_pool_assembler.py`: 17 passed; the new cases fail on `main`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
